FuzzMind Security Labs — PGP key not yet published.

Status:
  The long-term team PGP key has not been published to this URL yet.
  This file is an honest status stub — NOT a PGP key block — so that
  clients honoring RFC 9116 do not cache a malformed key.

How to contact us in the meantime:
  1. Email security@fuzzmind.com WITHOUT the sensitive details.
     Ask us to coordinate a secure channel. We will reply with an
     ephemeral public key or set up a Signal / Keybase handoff.
  2. /.well-known/security.txt has the `Encryption:` field commented
     out on purpose while this file is a stub, so automated VDP
     tooling will not treat /pgp.asc as a trust anchor.

How to publish the real key (for maintainers):
    bash scripts/gen-pgp.sh
  That script generates an Ed25519 + Curve25519 key on your local
  machine, writes the armored public half here, and leaves the secret
  key only in your local gpg keyring. Follow the printed next-steps
  to uncomment the Encryption line and back up the secret key to
  cold storage.

— fuzzmind.com / security@fuzzmind.com
